<section id="reader-cloud-sync" class="reader-cloud-sync" aria-labelledby="reader-cloud-sync-heading">
  <h3 id="reader-cloud-sync-heading">Cross-device reading sync</h3>
  <p>Keep your library and reading positions with your account. Your global reading appearance stays specific to each device.</p>
  <p id="reader-cloud-sync-status" class="fine" role="status" aria-live="polite">Sign in to manage your cloud library.</p>
  <p id="reader-bookmark-cloud-warning" class="fine" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>Paragraph bookmarks are safe on this device but do not fit in the cloud reading record. Remove older bookmarks if needed; other reading data can continue syncing.</p>
  <div class="account-actions">
    <button type="button" id="reader-sync-enable" class="button secondary" hidden>Enable sync and merge</button>
    <button type="button" id="reader-sync-now" class="button secondary" hidden>Sync now</button>
    <button type="button" id="reader-sync-pause" class="button secondary" hidden>Pause sync on this device</button>
  </div>
  <div id="reader-sync-conflict" class="reader-sync-conflict" hidden>
    <p id="reader-sync-conflict-detail"></p>
    <p class="fine">Choose which device's version wins only for conflicting books. Books present on just one device are preserved.</p>
    <div class="account-actions">
      <button type="button" class="button" data-sync-choice="device">Keep this device's position</button>
      <button type="button" class="button secondary" data-sync-choice="cloud">Keep cloud position</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="fine">Guests remain local. XP, ranks and verified rewards use separate, server-protected records and are never imported from your browser.</p>
</section>
